    <div class="hp-cover">
        <div class="hp-logo-bar hp-cover-overlay">
            <div class="container">
                <img src="{{ asset("images/hacker/logo-white.svg") }}" alt="Pardubický Hacker - logo">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="w-100 d-flex align-content-center justify-content-start justify-content-md-end container">
            <div class="hp-cover-headline text-left text-md-center">
                <p>
                    Are you a <b>primary school</b> pupil who enjoys <b>programming</b>?
                    <span class="d-inline-block">Are you just starting</span> with programming and want to learn more, or
                    are you a pro ready to take on the very best?
                </p>
                <p>
                    Pardubický Hacker - programming for primary schools has a <b>competition</b> part and a
                    <b>study</b> part. You can program in
                    <b>Python</b>, <b>Java</b>, <b>JavaScript</b>, <b>C</b>, <b>C++</b> or <b>C#</b>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hp-cover-details hp-cover-overlay">
            <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-md-row container">
                <div class="hp-cover-details-segment hp-cover-details-segment-larger">
                    <h2>Competition</h2>
                    <p>
                        Every month, 3 competition problems will be waiting for you. The system checks online whether
                        you solved a problem correctly. Whoever solves the problems first and in the fewest attempts
                        gets the most points. The points for the individual problems add up.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The competition has two semesters, winter and summer. Each semester has online rounds and an
                        in-person final held in Pardubice. The winter semester has 3 online rounds: October, November
                        and December, with the final in January. The summer semester has 4 online rounds: February,
                        March, April and May, with the final in June. You can join during the year too.
                    </p>

                    <a class="btn btn-lg btn-outline-light" href="{{ path('register') }}">
                        Sign up
                    </a>
                </div>

                <div class="hp-cover-details-segment">
                    <h2>On-line course</h2>
                    <p>
                        Every month we explain a programming topic and bring exercises to practise it. We try to
                        prepare exercises that will be interesting for you even if you can already program. You can
                        check whether your solution is correct online.
                    </p>

                    <a class="btn btn-lg btn-outline-light" href="https://github.com/delta-cs/seminar">
                        Start studying
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container mt-4">
        <div class="d-flex flex-row align-items-center">
            <h2 class="me-3">News</h2>
            <a class="btn btn-sm btn-info" href="{{ path('blog_list') }}">Read all</a>
        </div>

        <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-lg-2 row-cols-xl-3">
            {% for post in blogPosts %}
                {% include 'blog/partials/blog_post_on_homepage.html.twig' with {'post': post} %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
